## Step 1: Link Inventory Audit

### Step Definition
```yaml
title: "Link Inventory Audit"
description: "Map your current internal linking structure to understand how authority flows through your site. We'll identify orphan pages with no incoming links, analyze link distribution patterns, and reveal which pages are hoarding authority versus which are starved for it."
```

### Execution Instructions
```yaml
concept: "comprehensive link graph analysis"
action: "Crawl and analyze all internal links across the entire site structure"
implementation: "Scan all pages to map existing internal links, calculate incoming/outgoing link counts per page, identify orphaned pages, measure link depth from homepage, and create a visual representation of the current link architecture"
deliverable: "link-inventory-audit.md"
```

### Analysis Focus
- **Orphaned Pages**: Pages with 0 incoming internal links
- **Link Depth**: Distance from homepage (clicks required to reach page)
- **Link Equity Distribution**: Which pages have most incoming links
- **Hub Pages**: Pages with high outgoing link counts
- **Authority Sinks**: High-value pages with few incoming links

### Key Metrics to Calculate
```yaml
metrics:
  - total_pages: "Count of all pages discovered"
  - orphaned_pages: "Pages with no incoming internal links"
  - avg_internal_links_per_page: "Average number of internal links"
  - max_link_depth: "Deepest page distance from homepage"
  - top_linked_pages: "Pages with most incoming links (top 10)"
  - underlinked_pages: "High-value pages with <3 incoming links"
```

### Crawl Tools Recommendation
- **Screaming Frog SEO Spider**: Desktop crawl tool
- **Sitebulb**: Visual site architecture
- **Custom script**: Node.js crawler for dynamic sites
- **CMS plugins**: WordPress SEO plugins with link analysis

## Step 2: Strategic Link Opportunities

### Step Definition
```yaml
title: "Strategic Link Opportunities"
description: "Identify high-value pages that need authority boosts via internal links. We'll find contextual opportunities to strengthen topical clusters, connect related content, and prioritize pages based on conversion potential and search visibility goals."
```

### Execution Instructions
```yaml
concept: "strategic link placement for authority distribution"
action: "Identify pages that need more internal links and determine optimal source pages"
implementation: "Analyze page importance (conversion value, search traffic, business goals), identify topical clusters that need stronger connections, find contextually relevant pages that could link to target pages, and prioritize link opportunities by impact potential"
deliverable: "strategic-link-opportunities.md"
```

### Page Prioritization Framework

#### 1. Identify Target Pages (Pages Needing Links)
```yaml
criteria:
  high_priority:
    - "Money pages: product/service pages with conversion goals"
    - "High search volume pages ranking positions 11-20"
    - "Orphaned pages with valuable content"
    - "Topical pillar pages that need authority"
  medium_priority:
    - "Blog posts with high engagement but low visibility"
    - "Service pages in secondary markets"
    - "Resource pages with link-worthy content"
  low_priority:
    - "Informational content without conversion goals"
    - "Archive pages and category indexes"
```

#### 2. Identify Source Pages (Pages That Should Link)
```yaml
criteria:
  ideal_sources:
    - "High-authority pages (many incoming links)"
    - "High-traffic pages (lots of visitors)"
    - "Contextually relevant pages (same topic/cluster)"
    - "Hub pages (resource centers, guides)"
```

#### 3. Opportunity Scoring
```javascript
opportunityScore = (
  targetPageValue * 0.4 +        // Conversion/traffic value
  contextualRelevance * 0.3 +     // Topic alignment
  sourcePageAuthority * 0.2 +     // Source page link equity
  implementationEase * 0.1        // Difficulty to add link
) * 100

// Prioritize opportunities with score > 70
```

### Topical Cluster Mapping
```yaml
clusters:
  - cluster_name: "Roofing Services"
    pillar_page: "/roofing-services"
    supporting_pages:
      - "/shingle-roofing"
      - "/metal-roofing"
      - "/roof-repair"
    missing_connections: 
      - link_from: "/roof-repair" 
        link_to: "/shingle-roofing"
        reason: "Users repairing shingles should see shingle replacement options"
```

## Step 3: Anchor Text Optimization

### Step Definition
```yaml
title: "Anchor Text Optimization"
description: "Audit your existing anchor text patterns to ensure diversity and relevance. We'll design descriptive, keyword-rich anchors that signal topical relationships to search engines while maintaining natural language flow for users."
```

### Execution Instructions
```yaml
concept: "anchor text diversity and relevance optimization"
action: "Analyze current anchor text patterns and plan optimized anchor text strategy"
implementation: "Extract all existing anchor text, identify over-optimization or generic text (like 'click here'), analyze keyword distribution in anchors, plan diverse, descriptive anchor text that signals content relationships, and ensure natural language while incorporating target keywords"
deliverable: "anchor-text-optimization-plan.md"
```

### Anchor Text Best Practices

#### 1. Anchor Text Types Distribution
```yaml
recommended_distribution:
  exact_match: "10-15%"  # "roofing services"
  partial_match: "30-40%"  # "quality roofing services in Portland"
  branded: "15-20%"  # "Oregon Exterior Experts"
  generic: "10-15%"  # "learn more", "click here"
  naked_url: "5-10%"  # "https://site.com/page"
  descriptive: "20-30%"  # "guide to choosing roof materials"
```

#### 2. Avoid Over-Optimization
```yaml
red_flags:
  - exact_match_ratio > 40%: "Too many exact match anchors (spam signal)"
  - generic_ratio > 30%: "Too many 'click here' links (missed opportunity)"
  - single_keyword_dominance > 50%: "One keyword used in 50%+ of all anchors"
```

#### 3. Contextual Anchor Design
```yaml
principles:
  - "Anchor should describe destination page content"
  - "Include target keyword naturally in sentence"
  - "Use variations and synonyms, not repetition"
  - "Make anchor clickable phrase length (2-5 words ideal)"
  - "Avoid anchor text in ALL CAPS or excessive punctuation!!!"
```

### Example Anchor Text Matrix
```yaml
target_page: "/metal-roofing-installation"
anchor_variations:
  - "metal roofing installation services"
  - "install a metal roof"
  - "professional metal roofing"
  - "our metal roof installation process"
  - "metal roofing solutions"
  - "guide to metal roof installation"
```

## Step 4: Implementation Path

### Step Definition
```yaml
title: "Implementation Path"
description: "Design new link paths that enhance UX without disrupting your site's architecture. We'll create a non-invasive implementation roadmap that adds contextual links within existing content, respects user flows, and scales across content types—no footer spam, just strategic connections."
```

### Execution Instructions
```yaml
concept: "non-disruptive link implementation strategy"
action: "Create an implementation plan that adds strategic links while preserving UX and site architecture"
implementation: "Identify exact placement locations for new links (within content body, related content sections, contextual sidebars), specify which files need modification, ensure links enhance rather than disrupt user journey, maintain existing navigation patterns, plan for scalable linking patterns across content types, and provide technology-specific implementation guidance"
deliverable: "link-implementation-path.md"
```

### Implementation Principles

#### 1. Contextual Placement Zones
```yaml
placement_priorities:
  high_value:
    - "Within main content body (first 2 paragraphs)"
    - "Contextual mentions of related topics"
    - "After problem statement, before solution"
  medium_value:
    - "Related resources sidebar"
    - "End-of-content 'Read Next' sections"
    - "Author bio with topic expertise links"
  low_value:
    - "Footer navigation (generic links)"
    - "Breadcrumb navigation"
    - "Header menu (already exists)"
```

#### 2. Non-Disruptive Integration Rules
```yaml
rules:
  - "Never add more than 3-5 new internal links per page"
  - "Links must fit naturally in sentence structure"
  - "Don't interrupt critical conversion content with links"
  - "Don't add links to navigation elements (header/footer/sidebar nav)"
  - "Avoid link density >5% (5 links per 100 words)"
  - "Test on mobile: ensure links are tappable (48px min touch target)"
```

#### 3. Technology-Specific Implementation

##### Static HTML Sites
```html
<!-- Before -->
<p>Metal roofing is durable and long-lasting.</p>

<!-- After -->
<p><a href="/metal-roofing-installation">Metal roofing</a> is durable and long-lasting, making it ideal for <a href="/oregon-weather-roofing">Oregon's climate</a>.</p>
```

##### React/Component-Based
```jsx
// Create reusable InternalLink component
<InternalLink href="/metal-roofing-installation">
  Metal roofing
</InternalLink>

// Automatically adds:
// - rel="noopener" for security
// - Analytics tracking
// - Prefetching for performance
```

##### WordPress/CMS
```yaml
options:
  - "Use Advanced Custom Fields to add 'related_pages' meta field"
  - "Install Yoast SEO Premium for automatic internal linking suggestions"
  - "Create custom shortcode: [internal-link url='/page']text[/internal-link]"
  - "Use Link Whisper plugin for automated linking suggestions"
```

##### Content-Heavy Sites (Blogs)
```yaml
scalable_approach:
  - "Create 'related posts' taxonomy/tag system"
  - "Auto-generate contextual links based on shared tags"
  - "Use NLP to identify topic similarity (TF-IDF, embeddings)"
  - "Build link recommendation engine: 'Pages about X should link to Y'"
```

